## Third-party components

eezo does not yet redistribute any third-party code. No runtime dependency has
been selected and no build is published. As dependencies are adopted, their
attribution notices are recorded here.

Every dependency eezo adopts must be under an OSI-approved permissive licence
so that this file stays a list of attributions rather than a list of
obligations. Copyleft and source-available licences (GPL, LGPL, AGPL, MPL,
BUSL, FSL) are out of scope for the framework's own dependency tree, because
they would propagate terms to applications built on eezo that the MIT License
does not.
